) VALUES (
  591, 'pakistan-cnic-domicile-prc-application-guide', 'How to Apply for CNIC, Domicile & PRC in Pakistan: Step-by-Step Application Process, Required Documents & Fees', 'guides-and-resources', 'NADRA & District Administration', 'Citizenship & Quota Guide', 'All Provinces & Federal, Pakistan',
  'Matric / Intermediate / Graduation / General Public', 'Public Advisory & Checklist', 'Ongoing Evergreen Procedure', '2026-11-08', 'https://id.nadra.gov.pk', 1,
  'CD', 'Comprehensive 2026 procedural guide to obtaining your Computerized National Identity Card (CNIC/Smart NIC) from NADRA, District Domicile Certificate from the DC/AC Office, and Sindh PRC (Form C & D) with document checklists, fees, and dual-domicile rules.', '["> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Why These Three Documents Determine Your Career & Public Service Eligibility:**\n> In Pakistan''s public recruitment system, vacancies in federal ministries, autonomous corporations, defense institutions, and provincial departments are allocated strictly on constitutional quotas (Merit, Punjab, Sindh Rural, Sindh Urban, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Balochistan, Ex-FATA, Gilgit-Baltistan, and AJK). Your **CNIC** establishes your legal identity and 18+ citizenship; your **Domicile Certificate** determines which provincial or regional quota you compete under; and in Sindh, your **Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC on Form-D)** legally determines your Urban vs. Rural classification. Without properly issued, verified, and attested copies of these documents, test authorities and public service commissions will reject your application at the document scrutiny stage.","Whether you are a fresh matriculate preparing your first identity dossier or a university graduate preparing for [FPSC competitive exams](/jobs/fpsc-online-application-challan-form-32a-guide), [SPSC recruitment](/jobs/spsc-exam-preparation-screening-challan-guide), or the [National Job Portal (NJP)](/jobs/national-job-portal-njp-pakistan-application-guide), this step-by-step guide explains the legal frameworks, exact document checklists, official fee structures, and application workflows required to obtain all three documents without falling victim to touts, illegal dual-domicile penalties, or preventable scrutiny objections.","## Comparison of CNIC, Domicile, and PRC\n\nUnderstanding the legal scope and administrative difference between these three core citizen documents prevents costly confusion during job applications and university admissions:\n\n| Feature | Computerized National Identity Card (CNIC) | District Domicile Certificate | Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC Form-D) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Issuing Authority** | [National Database & Registration Authority (NADRA)](https://id.nadra.gov.pk) | Deputy Commissioner (DC) / District Administration | Deputy Commissioner / Assistant Commissioner (Sindh) |\n| **Governing Law** | NADRA Ordinance, 2000 & National Registration Rules | Pakistan Citizenship Act, 1951 (Section 17) & Rules 1952 | Sindh Permanent Residence Certificate Rules, 1971 |\n| **Primary Purpose** | Proof of identity, age, parentage, biometric record, and federal citizenship | Legal proof of permanent residence in a specific administrative district | Proves urban or rural status within Sindh for provincial quotas & medical/engineering seats |\n| **Validity** | 10 years (Normal Smart Card); Lifetime for senior citizens (60+) | Permanent (unless lawfully cancelled or transferred) | Permanent (unless cancelled due to fraudulent declaration) |\n| **Territorial Scope** | Nationwide (Federal jurisdiction across Pakistan and abroad) | Specific district within a designated province | Specific taluka/district within the province of Sindh |","## 1. How to Apply for CNIC / Smart NIC at NADRA\n\nEvery Pakistani citizen who attains 18 years of age is legally required to register with [NADRA](https://id.nadra.gov.pk) to obtain an identity card. For employment and recruitment purposes, always opt for the chip-based **Smart National Identity Card (SNIC)**, as it integrates biometric verification and is universally scanned by government commission testing centers.\n\n### A. First-Time Application Requirements (Age 18+)\nTo apply for a fresh Smart CNIC at any NADRA Registration Center (NRC) or Executive Center, you must present:\n1. **Original Child Registration Certificate (CRC / Form-B)** issued by NADRA.\n2. **Original CNIC of one blood relative** (Father, Mother, or real Brother/Sister) who must be physically present at the counter for biometric fingerprint verification.\n3. If no blood relative can be present, you must obtain a computerized **Biometric Attestation Form (Form-MN)** from the counter and have it attested by a Gazetted Government Officer (BPS-17+) or elected local representative before submission.\n4. **Matriculation Certificate / Sanad:** Highly recommended to carry your original Matric marksheet/certificate to ensure your date of birth, name, and father''s name spellings are recorded exactly identical to your academic credentials.\n\n### B. Application Workflow at the NADRA Center\n- **Token Generation:** Present your Form-B at the reception desk to receive an entry token.\n- **Biometrics & Photo:** Proceed to the data acquisition counter for live digital photography, ten-finger biometric fingerprint scanning, and digital iris scan.\n- **Data Verification:** The data entry operator enters your particulars into the system. **Crucial Step:** Double-check the preview screen. Ensure your name, father''s name, permanent address, and date of birth match your school records character-for-character.\n- **Print Form & Signature:** Review the printed Urdu and English registration form, verify every entry, and sign or provide your thumb impression.\n- **Token Slip Collection:** Pay the prescribed government fee at the cashier and collect your tracking slip carrying your 12-digit tracking ID.\n\n### C. Pak-ID Mobile App & Web Portal\nIf you already possess a CNIC and need a **Renewal** (for expired cards), **Modification** (marital status or address change), or **Duplicate** (for lost cards), you do not need to stand in physical queues. Download the official **Pak-ID Mobile App** (available on Android and iOS). The app uses your smartphone camera for biometric fingerprint scanning, document uploads, and digital photo capture, delivering the renewed card directly to your doorstep via Pakistan Post urgent courier.\n\n### D. Official NADRA Fee Structure & Processing Times\n- **Normal Smart Card:** Rs. 750 (Delivery in 31 working days).\n- **Urgent Smart Card:** Rs. 1,500 (Delivery in 15 working days).\n- **Executive Smart Card:** Rs. 2,500 (Delivery in 7 working days at Executive Centers).\n- *Note: Fee rates are verified against official NADRA scheduled notifications. Track your delivery status online using your 12-digit Tracking ID at id.nadra.gov.pk.*","## 2. How to Obtain a District Domicile Certificate\n\nUnder Section 17 of the **Pakistan Citizenship Act, 1951**, a Domicile Certificate is conclusive legal evidence of a person''s permanent residence in a specific province and district. Because federal and provincial recruitment quotas in Pakistan are allocated based on district population ratios, every government job applicant must hold an unassailable domicile.\n\n### A. Where to Apply\nApplications for Domicile Certificates are processed through the office of the **Deputy Commissioner (DC)**, **Assistant Commissioner (AC)**, or designated **Citizen Facilitation Centers (e-Khidmat Markaz in Punjab, Service Sindh Centers, or Citizen Facilitation Centers in KP and Balochistan)** of your native district.\n\n### B. Required Document Dossier\nBefore visiting the DC office, organize the following documents into a clean folder:\n- **Application Form P-1:** Prescribed statutory application form, available at the DC office stamp vendor or downloadable from the respective provincial revenue portal.\n- **Photographs:** Four recent passport-size photographs with a clean light blue background.\n- **CNIC Photocopies:** Attested copies of the applicant''s valid CNIC (or Form-B if under 18) and attested CNIC copies of both parents.\n- **Father''s Domicile:** Attested copy of father''s Domicile Certificate (or guardian''s domicile along with death certificate if father is deceased).\n- **Academic Proof:** Attested copies of Matriculation Certificate / Secondary School Certificate (SSC) showing date of birth and district of schooling.\n- **Proof of District Residence (Crucial):** Any of the following verified proofs:\n  - Registered property ownership deed / Fard Jamabandi / Form VII (in rural revenue areas).\n  - Municipal property tax receipt or registered rent lease agreement.\n  - Electricity, Sui gas, or PTCL landline utility bill of the residence (last 3 consecutive months).\n- **Affidavit on Non-Judicial Stamp Paper:** A sworn declaration attested by an Oath Commissioner or Notary Public affirming that:\n  1. The applicant is a permanent resident of the specified district.\n  2. The applicant has abandoned residence in any previous place.\n  3. The applicant **does not hold any other domicile certificate** in any other district or province of Pakistan.\n\n### C. Revenue Verification & Field Scrutiny\n1. **Submission & Token:** Submit the completed Form P-1 and dossier at the facilitation counter or revenue branch.\n2. **Field Verification:** The file is marked to the area **Tapedar / Patwari** and **Tehsildar / Mukhtiarkar** for physical verification of permanent residence and electoral list entry.\n3. **Police / Special Branch Verification:** In sensitive or border districts, a local police station report verifies character and continuous residence.\n4. **Final Approval:** Following favorable revenue reports, the Assistant Commissioner or Deputy Commissioner approves and signs the official Domicile Certificate bearing the embossed district seal.\n5. **Timeline & Official Fees:** Official court fee stamps typically range between Rs. 100 and Rs. 500 depending on the province. Processing takes approximately 7 to 14 working days.","## 3. Sindh Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC Form-C and Form-D)\n\nFor candidates competing in Sindh provincial departments, [Sindh Public Service Commission (SPSC)](/jobs/spsc-exam-preparation-screening-challan-guide) competitive examinations, and public sector medical/engineering colleges, holding a Domicile alone is **insufficient**. You must also hold a **Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC)** governed by the Sindh Permanent Residence Certificate Rules, 1971.\n\n### A. Distinction Between Form-C and Form-D\n- **PRC on Form-C:** Issued primarily for academic admissions, institutional scholarships, and educational grants.\n- **PRC on Form-D:** Issued specifically for **employment and government service recruitment**. It proves whether the candidate belongs to the **Sindh Urban** (Karachi, Hyderabad, and Sukkur municipal corporations) or **Sindh Rural** quota.\n\n### B. Required Documents for Sindh PRC Form-D\n1. Prescribed PRC Application Form.\n2. Two attested copies of the applicant''s District Domicile Certificate.\n3. Attested copies of CNIC (applicant and father).\n4. Four passport-size photographs.\n5. **Proof of Continuous Education in Sindh:** Primary, Middle, and Matriculation school leaving certificates or character certificates proving continuous schooling within the district.\n6. Father''s PRC Form-D (or evidence of continuous residence of father/guardian in Sindh for at least 15 years prior to application).\n7. Electoral roll (voter list) entry certificate from the District Election Commissioner verifying family registration in the relevant union council.\n8. Sworn non-judicial affidavit stating applicant will reside permanently in the district.","## 4. The Single-Domicile Law & Severe Legal Penalties\n\nA common pitfall among job seekers in Pakistan is attempting to acquire domiciles in multiple districts—for example, obtaining one domicile in an interior rural district to gain quota advantages, and another in a major metropolitan city for schooling or bank loans.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **Holding Dual Domiciles is a Serious Criminal Offense:**\n> Under Section 17 of the Pakistan Citizenship Act and the rulings of the Supreme Court of Pakistan, **no citizen can hold more than one domicile at the same time**. \n> - If an applicant is discovered holding two domiciles, **both domicile certificates are automatically cancelled**.\n> - The candidate is permanently debarred from federal and provincial public service commission recruitments.\n> - Criminal charges under **Section 193 of the Pakistan Penal Code (PPC)** for submitting a false declaration before public authorities can be initiated, carrying potential imprisonment.\n> - If you move permanently to a new district, you must formally surrender your previous domicile to the issuing DC office and obtain an official **Surrender Certificate / NOC** before applying for a fresh domicile in your new district.","## 5. Summary Checklist: Documents Required Before Applying\n\nKeep this handy reference table saved when preparing your citizen dossier:\n\n| Stage / Document | Key Requirements | Verification Source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **NADRA Smart CNIC** | Form-B + Blood relative with CNIC + Matric certificate | [NADRA Registration Center / Pak-ID App](https://id.nadra.gov.pk) |\n| **District Domicile** | Form P-1 + 4 Photos + Residence proof + Tax/Utility bills + Affidavit | DC / AC Office / e-Khidmat / Citizen Facilitation Center |\n| **Sindh PRC Form-D** | Domicile copy + 10-year education certificates + Father PRC + Voter record | District Administration / Assistant Commissioner Office |\n| **Degree & Transcript** | Clean photocopies matching CNIC spelling exactly | Attestation by BPS-17+ Gazetted Officer |\n| **Master Application File** | Transparent plastic sleeves + scanned PDF copies (300 DPI) | [Government Jobs Documents Checklist Guide](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026) |","## 6. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\n\n### What should I do if the spelling of my name on my CNIC does not match my Matric certificate?\nYour Matriculation (Secondary School Certificate) issued by the Board of Intermediate and Secondary Education (BISE) is considered your primary legal birth record by government recruiting bodies. If your CNIC has a different spelling or incorrect date of birth, visit a NADRA Registration Center immediately with your original Matric Sanad to apply for a **Data Modification**. Never apply for government vacancies with mismatched names, as this leads to rejection during scrutiny.\n\n### Can an expired CNIC be used to take an FPSC, SPSC, or NTS screening test?\nNo. Test centers strictly require a valid, unexpired original CNIC for gate entry and biometric verification. If your card has expired, apply for renewal immediately and carry the original stamped **NADRA Renewal Token Slip** alongside your expired card, passport, or original driving license as secondary photo identification.\n\n### How can I verify if my Domicile Certificate is genuine and registered in DC office records?\nMost provincial revenue departments (such as Punjab e-Khidmat and Sindh e-Revenue) now feature digital barcode verification. For older manual certificates, you can submit an application for **Verification / Attestation** to the Revenue Branch of the issuing Deputy Commissioner Office, where clerks verify the certificate number against the permanent district domicile register.\n\n### If my parents do not have a domicile from my current district, can I still apply?\nYes, provided you have attained 18 years of age and can prove continuous permanent residence in the district for the statutory period (typically 3 to 5 years depending on provincial rules) through registered property deeds, municipal residency proofs, continuous local schooling records, and utility billing records. You must also furnish a surrender affidavit explaining why you are not claiming your parents'' district of origin.\n\n### Does a Domicile Certificate expire after a certain number of years?\nNo. A Domicile Certificate has lifetime validity unless the holder formally applies to transfer and surrender it to another district, or unless it is revoked by the Deputy Commissioner on grounds of fraud, misrepresentation, or dual-domicile violation. However, older manual paper certificates without photographs should be updated to computerized/smart domicile cards where available to prevent authenticity objections.","> [!TIP]\n> **Check Your Application Readiness Before Applying:**\n> Use CareerDost''s free interactive [Government Job Application Readiness Checker](/tools/job-readiness-checker) to verify your CNIC, domicile, educational transcripts, and age limit eligibility before submitting applications for federal and provincial government posts."]', 'How to Apply for CNIC, Domicile & PRC in Pakistan (2026 Guide)', 'Step-by-step 2026 procedure for obtaining your CNIC from NADRA, Domicile Certificate from Deputy Commissioner office, and Sindh PRC with fees and document lists.', datetime('now'),
  datetime('now'), 'published', '/images/pakistan-cnic-domicile-prc-application-guide.webp', 'Pakistani citizenship application documents including CNIC, domicile folder, and official forms on a wooden desk', 'Not Applicable (Citizen Procedure)', 'Comprehensive Public Guide',
  'https://id.nadra.gov.pk', 1, 'how to apply for cnic domicile prc in pakistan', 'https://careerdost.blog/jobs/pakistan-cnic-domicile-prc-application-guide', 'How to Apply for CNIC, Domicile & PRC in Pakistan — Step-by-Step Guide', 'Complete 2026 guide to obtaining your CNIC from NADRA, District Domicile Certificate from the DC Office, and Sindh PRC (Form C & D) with document checklists and fees.', 1
)
